# Governance Hierarchy

Methodology Governance

Govern the HCGO Enterprise Architecture methodology.

Responsibilities include:

- Methodology structure
- Methodology progression
- Architectural phase integration
- Architectural dependency management
- Cross-phase traceability
- Methodology integrity
- Methodology consistency

↓

Enterprise Governance

Govern the enterprise.

Responsibilities include:

- Enterprise principles
- Enterprise authority
- Enterprise ownership
- Enterprise stewardship
- Enterprise semantics
- Enterprise governance
- Enterprise architecture

↓

Implementation Governance

Govern the faithful implementation of the approved Enterprise Architecture.

Responsibilities include:

- Implementation conformance
- Architectural compliance
- Deployment governance
- Operational implementation

Each governance layer possesses a unique constitutional responsibility.

No governance layer replaces the authority of another.

---

# Constitutional Principle

Governance exists at multiple constitutional levels.

Methodology Governance governs the methodology.

Enterprise Governance governs the enterprise.

Implementation Governance governs the faithful realization of the approved Enterprise Architecture.

Each governance layer preserves the authoritative outcomes established by the governance layer above it.

Authority is neither duplicated nor transferred between governance levels.

---

# Enterprise Principle

Enterprise Architecture is an integrated constitutional methodology.

Each architectural phase owns the authoritative decisions established within that phase.

Subsequent architectural phases faithfully represent and integrate those decisions.

Architectural integration never transfers architectural authority.

Technology faithfully implements the integrated Enterprise Architecture.

No architectural or implementation artifact may redefine authoritative decisions established by an earlier approved architectural phase.

---

# Architecture Outcome

The Enterprise Architecture Integration Model becomes the authoritative constitutional model describing how every Enterprise Architecture phase integrates across HCGO.

It establishes complete architectural traceability from Constitutional Governance through Enterprise Service Architecture.

Technology Implementation begins only after Enterprise Architecture has been completed, approved, and formally baselined.

This establishes the constitutional transition between Enterprise Architecture and Technology Implementation.

The Enterprise Architecture Integration Model governs the methodology.

It does not govern the enterprise.

It does not govern implementation.

